   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2020-07-21",
   "text": "Slave-Free Business Certification Act of 2020\n\n This bill requires businesses with annual revenue greater than $500 million to audit their supply chains for labor practices or human trafficking activities that violate specified national or international standards and report the results to the Department of Labor."
  }
